body: "## Observed documentation mismatch\n\nThe official [`@unbrained/pm-case@2026.11.6` npm release](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@unbrained/pm-case/v/2026.11.6) is live, but its checksum-verified tarball README and the [default-branch README](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case#install) still describe the candidate as local and unpublished. The archive-building route comes first; ordinary npm/Bun installation is described as a future step.\n\nOn Node 24.22.1 I installed the verified published PM Case and PM CLI 2026.11.16 tarballs in a fresh npm consumer, activated the installed extension in a disposable non-Git tracker, and successfully created a model and proposed/selected the four cases in a 2×2 fixture. The package works through the scoped coordinate and the `pm case` extension identity; no runtime or npm availability defect is implied. The stale opening can nevertheless send users or agents through a source checkout and pack workflow they do not need.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Lead with a fresh npm/Bun consumer and scoped registry installation today; preserve the separate tracker activation step, the `npm:` prefix for registry activation through PM, and the fact that there is no standalone binary.\n- Keep source checkout, archive review and prepublication instructions only as an explicitly optional maintainer path.\n- Check the rendered GitHub and the next actually published npm README; a successful git merge alone does not update the current registry artifact.\n- Preserve the no-Git pack/activation and command smoke coverage.\n\nRelated shipped publication work: [PR #14](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/14) and its [scoped registry tracking item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/blob/main/.agents/pm/chores/pm-case-scoped-npm-name.toon). This is a post-publication documentation follow-up, not a request to republish or rename.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-16T10:37:43Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-case#14 - Publish the package to npm as `@unbrained/pm-case` [closed]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-19T06:21:51Z)\n>\n> New evidence for the archive fallback in this issue: [release preparation run 44462023939](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/44462023939/job/135350999392) failed the documented archive-install test in `test/review-classes.test.ts`.\n> \n> At [`b0ea60a`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/commit/b0ea60a62cd9b63f5a3b3cdad5f38b4a0de37de1), the README names `unbrained-pm-case-2026.11.6.tgz`, while the test constructs the filename from the candidate version. In a clean temporary directory, the same README shell prefix with `npm` stubbed to check file existence passed with the `.11.6` archive and failed with only the `.11.19` archive. This isolates the path mismatch, not npm itself.\n> \n> Keep the fresh consumer smoke check and verify it also passes after a version bump, with the optional archive instructions using the actual packed filename."
